Verse 1:
[G]There’s sunshine [C]in my soul tod[G]ay,
More [D7]glorious and [G]br[C]ig[G]ht
Than glows in [C]any earthly [G]sky,
For [D]Jesus [A7]is my [D]light.
[D7]O there’s [G]sunshine, [C]blessed [G]sunshine,
When the peaceful, happy moments [D]roll
[D7]When [G]Jesus [C]shows [G]His [C]smiling [G]face
There [C]is [G]sunshine [D7]in the [G]soul.

Refrain:
[G]O [C]there's sunshine, [G]blessed sunshine,
[D7]When [G]the peaceful, [C]happy [G]moments roll
[C]When Jesus shows [G]His smiling face
[D]There is [A7]sunshine in [D]the soul.

Verse 2:
[G]There's music [C]in my [G]soul today,
[D7]A [G]carol [C]to [G]my King,
[C]And Jesus, [G]listening, can hear
[D]The [A7]songs I [D]cannot sing.

Verse 3:
[G]There's springtime [C]in my [G]soul today,
[D7]For [G]when the [C]Lord [G]is near,
[C]The dove of peace [G]sings in my heart,
[D]The [A7]flowers of [D]grace appear.

Verse 4:
[G]Theres gladness [C]in my [G]soul today,
[D7]And [G]hope, and [C]praise, [G]and love,
[C]For blessings which [G]He gives me now,
[D]For [A7]joys "laid [D]up" above.
